        "original_id": "53b71402-1228-5d83-bad8-b175f6151be9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mykhailo Pylypovych Kravchuk, Israel Gelfand, Victor Lidskii, Natalia Morar\n- Organizations: Moscow State University\n- Roles: mathematician, adviser, sociology student\n- Places: Ukraine, Moldova, Russia\n\nFacts:\n- Mykhailo Pylypovych Kravchuk, also Krawtchouk, was a Soviet Ukrainian mathematician born on September 27, 1892 and died on March 9, 1942.\n- Mykhailo Pylypovych Kravchuk authored around 180 articles on mathematics despite his early death.\n- Israel Gelfand was a prominent Soviet mathematician born on 2 September 1913 and died on 5 October 2009.\n- Israel Gelfand was the adviser of Victor Lidskii at Moscow State University.\n- Natalia Morar was born in Moldova and moved to Russia in 2002 to study sociology at Moscow State University.\n- Natalia Morar graduated from Moscow State University in 2007.",
